---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const contactEmail = "privacy@owlfoundry.org";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | OwlFoundry"
  description="Learn how OwlFoundry collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-effective-date">Effective August 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how OwlFoundry ("OwlFoundry," "we," "us,"
        or "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information when
        you use our websites and hosted online services that link to this policy
        (collectively, the "Services").
      </p>
      <p>
        Open-source software published by OwlFoundry may be installed and
        operated by third parties. This policy does not cover independently
        operated or self-hosted deployments. The operator of such a deployment
        is responsible for its own privacy practices.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="information-we-collect">
        <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>

        <h3>Information you provide</h3>
        <p>
          We may collect information you submit directly, such as your email
          address, account details, support requests, and other communications.
        </p>

        <h3>Google OAuth information</h3>
        <p>
          If you choose to sign in with Google, we receive only your Google
          account identifier, name, email address, and profile image. We do not
          request access to content in Google products such as Gmail, Drive,
          Calendar, or Contacts.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use these fields to authenticate you, create or connect your
          account, display your profile, provide account support, protect your
          account and the Services, and comply with law. We store them as part
          of your account record and retain them as described in the Data
          retention section below.
        </p>
        <p>
          We share these fields only with service providers acting on our behalf
          to host, secure, or operate the Services; when you direct us to do so;
          when required by law or necessary to protect rights and safety; or as
          part of a corporate transaction subject to appropriate safeguards. The
          general use and sharing provisions below do not authorize any broader
          use or disclosure of Google OAuth information.
        </p>

        <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
        <p>
          When you use the Services, we may collect technical and usage
          information such as your IP address, browser and device type, request
          timestamps, pages or features used, and diagnostic or security events.
          We may also use cookies or similar technologies that are necessary for
          authentication, security, and user preferences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-we-use-information">
        <h2 id="how-we-use-information">How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use personal information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>provide, operate, and maintain the Services;</li>
          <li>authenticate users and manage accounts;</li>
          <li>respond to support requests and other communications;</li>
          <li>monitor reliability, prevent abuse, and protect security;</li>
          <li>improve the Services; and</li>
          <li>comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="google-api-data">
        <h2 id="google-api-data">Google API data</h2>
        <p>
          Our use and transfer to any other application of information received
          from Google APIs will adhere to the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use information received from Google APIs for advertising,
          and we do not sell that information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-we-share-information">
        <h2 id="how-we-share-information">How we share information</h2>
        <p>We may share personal information only as needed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            with service providers that process information on our behalf to
            host, secure, support, or operate the Services;
          </li>
          <li>
            when you direct us to share it or connect a third-party service;
          </li>
          <li>
            to comply with law, legal process, or valid government requests, or
            to protect rights, safety, and the integrity of the Services; and
          </li>
          <li>
            in connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization,
            or sale of assets, subject to appropriate safeguards.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not share it
          for cross-context behavioral advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention">
        <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably
          necessary to provide the Services, maintain security and business
          records, resolve disputes, and meet legal obligations. Retention
          periods vary according to the type of information and why we process
          it. We delete or de-identify information when it is no longer needed,
          unless the law requires us to retain it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="choices">
        <h2 id="choices">Your choices and requests</h2>
        <p>
          You may ask to access, correct, or delete your personal information or
          account by emailing{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Depending on
          where you live, you may have additional privacy rights. We may need to
          verify your identity before fulfilling a request.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can review or revoke OwlFoundry's access to your Google account at
          any time from your{" "}
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">
            Google Account connections
          </a>. Revoking access stops future access but does not automatically
          delete information already stored by the Services. Contact us to
          request deletion.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="security">
        <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable technical and organizational measures designed to
          protect personal information. No method of transmission or storage is
          completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="international-transfers">
        <h2 id="international-transfers">International data transfers</h2>
        <p>
          The Services and our service providers may process information in
          countries other than your own. Where required, we use appropriate
          safeguards for international transfers of personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="children">
        <h2 id="children">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The Services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not
          knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you
          believe a child has provided us with personal information, contact us
          so that we can take appropriate action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="policy-changes">
        <h2 id="policy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. We will publish the
          updated version on this page and revise the effective date. If changes
          materially affect your rights, we will provide additional notice when
          reasonably practicable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact-us">
        <h2 id="contact-us">Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
